# Browser targets for the build.
#
# These targets cover every browser that can render the site at all. The oldest
# (Safari 15.4, March 2022) already supports every modern JS feature the app
# uses, so nothing regresses by declaring them.
#
# NOTE, honest limitation: this does NOT remove the ~14 KiB "Legacy JavaScript"
# chunk Lighthouse reports. That chunk is Next.js's own polyfill bundle, which
# is injected unconditionally (not nomodule-gated) and is not driven by
# browserslist. Verified after adding this file: the runtime feature-detects for
# Array.prototype.at, Object.fromEntries, trimStart/trimEnd et al. are still in
# the output. Removing them would mean patching the framework's bundling, which
# is not worth 14 KiB.
#
# This file still earns its place: it governs CSS autoprefixing and any
# browserslist-aware tooling added later, and it documents the support floor.
#
# Deliberately NOT supporting IE11: it cannot run the React 19 runtime.

